{"id": "86247", "name": "מעגל – משיק ונורמל בנקודה, מעגל סביב הראשית (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Find the equations of the tangent and normal to the circle</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} \\]</p><p>at the point \\(({{CT:1}},{{CT:2}})\\).</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">Tangent: [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:10px\"></div><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">Normal: [[input:ans2]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans2]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> The tangent is obtained from the tangent formula of an ellipse (a circle is a special case); the normal is the line through the point perpendicular to the tangent.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The tangent</b><br>Circles are a special case of the ellipse centred at \\((x_c,y_c)\\)<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{(x-x_c)^2}{a^2}+\\frac{(y-y_c)^2}{b^2}=1. \\]</p>The tangent to this ellipse, through the point \\((x',y')\\), is given by<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{(x-x_c)(x'-x_c)}{a^2}+\\frac{(y-y_c)(y'-y_c)}{b^2}=1. \\]</p>In our case we have \\(a^2=b^2={{CT:3}}\\) and \\(x'={{CT:1}}\\) and \\(y'={{CT:2}}\\). Using these values we have the tangent line as<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:4}} \\]</p>Expanding and rearranging give<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:5}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The normal</b><br>A line through \\((x',y')\\) with gradient \\(m\\) has equation<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y=m(x-x')+y'. \\]</p>If a line has gradient \\(m\\) then the perpendicular line has gradient \\(-1/m\\). Our tangent line has gradient {{CT:6}}, so the normal line through \\(({{CT:1}},{{CT:2}})\\) has equation<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y= {{CT:7}} = {{CT:8}}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>Tangent: [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>Normal: [[feedback:prt2]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "ta1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The equation for your tangent is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The equation for your tangent is incorrect.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "ta2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The equation for your normal is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The equation for your normal is incorrect.</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["ac", "ap", "bc", "bp", "p", "pm", "q", "rs", "ta1", "ta2", "tas1", "tas2"], "nvariants": 1}